# The overworld's conifer, standing on a tree tile inside the playable area.
#
# Y is up, +Z is north, one world unit is one map tile. The lowest vertex sits
# on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0, so the game places it
# by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which is
# what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. Get it backwards and the
# model still draws, it just goes flat ambient dark. The ring convention is
# pine.obj's: (r cos t, y, r sin t) with the angle increasing, cones wound
# apex then ring[i] then ring[i+1], and the trunk's quads wound top[i],
# bottom[i], bottom[i+1], top[i+1].
#
# Two overlapping six sided cones and a four sided trunk: exactly 20
# triangles, 2.45 units tall. That budget is the whole reason this file
# exists rather than the overworld reusing pine.obj, which is 26.
#
# The two are drawn in different places on purpose. pine.obj is the battle
# backdrop, where five trees are the only scenery in the shot and can afford
# a third cone. Here a screenful of Route 1 can hold nineteen of these, so
# the third cone would cost 114 triangles to add detail that is eight pixels
# tall. The silhouette is deliberately the same: a player walking a route and
# then fighting on it should be looking at one forest.
#
# The trees that frame the map are not these. Those are still the sprites in
# art/build_art.py, because the border is over a hundred tiles of tree and
# geometry there would cost more than everything else in the frame put
# together. tools/picomon_data.py decides which is which by flooding inward
# from the map edge, so the split is level data and not a guess made per
# frame.

mtllib treepine.mtl

# upper cone: apex, then its ring
v 0.000 2.450 0.000
v 0.420 1.350 0.000
v 0.210 1.350 0.364
v -0.210 1.350 0.364
v -0.420 1.350 0.000
v -0.210 1.350 -0.364
v 0.210 1.350 -0.364

# lower cone: apex sits inside the upper cone so the two read as one tree
v 0.000 1.700 0.000
v 0.600 0.580 0.000
v 0.300 0.580 0.520
v -0.300 0.580 0.520
v -0.600 0.580 0.000
v -0.300 0.580 -0.520
v 0.300 0.580 -0.520

# the trunk, top ring then bottom ring
v 0.110 0.660 0.000
v 0.000 0.660 0.110
v -0.110 0.660 0.000
v -0.000 0.660 -0.110
v 0.130 0.000 0.000
v 0.000 0.000 0.130
v -0.130 0.000 0.000
v -0.000 0.000 -0.130

usemtl pine_needles
f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
f 1 4 5
f 1 5 6
f 1 6 7
f 1 7 2
f 8 9 10
f 8 10 11
f 8 11 12
f 8 12 13
f 8 13 14
f 8 14 9

usemtl pine_bark
f 15 19 20 16
f 16 20 21 17
f 17 21 22 18
f 18 22 19 15
